panel.innerHTML=`<div class="vt-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">BTR / ADAPTIVE EVENT STUDIO</span><h2>See the game<em> like a coach.</em></h2><p>A broadcast-style synthetic training minute with automatic player, ball, pass and shot-candidate detection. Every event carries source frames, evidence support and a declared limit.</p></div><span class="vt-local">ADAPTIVE TRACKING ON DEVICE · AI EDITOR OPTIONAL</span></div><div class="vt-layout"><div class="vt-main"><div class="vt-screen"><div class="vt-camera"><video playsinline preload="metadata" poster="assets/tracking/poster.jpg?v=141" aria-label="One-minute synthetic training match"><source src="assets/tracking/training-minute.mp4?v=141" type="video/mp4"></video><canvas class="vt-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></canvas></div><div class="vt-analysis-badge"><b>AUTO EVENTING</b><span>PIXEL-DERIVED · SYNTHETIC</span></div><span class="vt-source">CALIBRATED BROADCAST CAMERA</span></div><div class="vt-controls"><button class="red-button" data-action="start">▶ Analyze the full minute</button><button class="outline-button" data-action="pause">Pause / resume</button><button class="outline-button" data-action="camera" aria-pressed="false">Broadcast close-up</button><button class="outline-button" data-action="reset">Reset</button><label><input type="checkbox" data-option="labels" checked> Player names</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-option="trails" checked> Movement trails</label></div><p class="vt-status" role="status">Loading calibration and pass-quality model…</p><div class="vt-health" aria-label="Live detector health"><div class="vt-health-title"><span>LIVE DETECTOR HEALTH</span><b data-health="state">WAITING</b></div><div class="vt-health-grid"><article><small>FRAME SUPPORT</small><strong data-health="confidence">—</strong><i><span data-health-bar="confidence"></span></i></article><article><small>EXPOSURE MODE</small><strong data-health="lighting">—</strong><p data-health="adaptation">Standard RGB</p></article><article><small>IDENTITY COVERAGE</small><strong data-health="coverage">—</strong><i><span data-health-bar="coverage"></span></i></article><article><small>LATEST EVENT</small><strong data-health="event">WAITING</strong><p data-health="event-note">Needs observed release and receipt</p></article></div><div class="vt-inference-line"><span>PIXELS</span><i></i><span>TRACKS</span><i></i><span>POSSESSION</span><i></i><span>EVENT</span><i></i><span>STORY</span></div></div><div class="vt-stats"></div><div class="vt-controls"><button class="outline-button" data-evidence="centre" disabled>Match Centre · this moment</button><button class="outline-button" data-evidence="truth" disabled>Truth Lab · this evidence</button></div><article class="vt-moment"><span class="eyebrow">THE NEXT STORY STARTS WITH EVIDENCE</span><h3>Press play. Let the pixels speak.</h3><p>Passes and shot candidates appear only after the ball movement is observed.</p></article><details class="vt-method"><summary>Challenge the detector / inspect its assumptions</summary><div class="vt-controls"><label><input type="checkbox" data-option="occludeBall"> Hide the ball from the detector</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-option="hideTracking"> Withhold player markers</label></div><p>These controls remove evidence before detection results reach event inference. Changing them resets the current analysis. A brief ball occlusion pauses inference for 0.3 seconds; a longer loss withholds the event instead of filling the gap from the known schedule.</p><p>Names come from enrolled coloured kit markers—not face recognition. The detector switches from exact RGB classification to illumination-tolerant chromatic matching in low light and exposes that mode in Detector Health. The fixed camera remains calibrated to a 105 × 68 m pitch.</p><p>Every inferred pass or shot candidate includes a heuristic evidence-support tier and exact frame range. Support is not a calibrated probability. Ball speed is a ground-plane trajectory estimate; aerial balls and moving cameras remain unsupported. Shot candidates do not certify goals.</p><p>Pass difficulty is a logistic model trained on synthetic outcomes using release-time distance, nearest defender and lane clearance. It is not a calibrated professional-football completion probability. This demo analyzes its own marked training footage; it does not automatically analyze the cinematic film.</p></details></div><aside class="vt-side"><div class="vt-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Tracking detail"><button data-tab="story" aria-pressed="true">Discussion</button><button data-tab="events" aria-pressed="false">Events</button><button data-tab="players" aria-pressed="false">Players</button><button data-tab="proof" aria-pressed="false">Validation</button></div><div class="vt-side-content"></div><button class="outline-button vt-export" disabled>Export observed evidence ↓</button></aside></div>`;
